Subject: [PATCH] SAGIT: print GIC state from the CPU startup timeout panic

The five second timeout now fires, but the IOLog diagnostics scroll off the
console before the panic screen appears.  Put the same readback into the
panic string so a photo of the panic screen carries the full picture.
---
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
@@ -202,5 +202,13 @@
 			if (now > deadline || waited_ms >= 5000) {
+				uint32_t g[7];
+				sweet_gic_sample(g);
 				IOLog("SWEET CPU: cpu=%u mpidr=0x%x NOT alive after 5s\n",
 				    i, topology->cpus[i].phys_id);
-				panic("SWEET CPU: cpu=%u startup timeout (reset/MMU/GIC/SGI)", i);
+				panic("SWEET CPU cpu=%u dead t=%u hp=0x%llx\n"
+				    "GICD ctlr=0x%x GICR grp=0x%x mod=0x%x en=0x%x pnd=0x%x waker=0x%x\n"
+				    "ICC sre=0x%llx g1=0x%llx pmr=0x%llx daif=0x%llx",
+				    i, waited_ms, __builtin_arm_rsr64("ICC_HPPIR1_EL1") & 0xFFFFFFULL,
+				    g[0], g[1], g[2], g[3], g[5], g[4],
+				    __builtin_arm_rsr64("ICC_SRE_EL1"), __builtin_arm_rsr64("ICC_IGRPEN1_EL1"),
+				    __builtin_arm_rsr64("ICC_PMR_EL1"), __builtin_arm_rsr64("DAIF"));
 			}
 			sweet_spin_us(1000);
